From: Nikhil Gurram <nikhgurr@qti.qualcomm.com>
Subject: [PATCH] pwhm: consolidate MLO link reconfiguration and cleanup

Preserve link-scoped MLO reconfiguration, primary-link promotion,
enabled-link restoration, empty-MLD cleanup, and logical hostapd anchor
removal. Exclude a departing link from primary election and retain the
remaining links in their original MLD.

When a moved primary owns the runtime anchor name, serialize removal of
only that runtime MLD using verified interface names and link IDs. Persist
the retained MLD owner across independent radio FSM callbacks, restore its
replacement primary first, and queue siblings only after that add succeeds.
Save all retained links' configured state before selecting the primary.

Keep remove/add retries local to the affected MLD and avoid radio or shared
hostapd restarts for these operations. Defer MBSSID transmitter removal when
unrelated MLDs depend on it. Radio-wide operations and genuine daemon
failure recovery retain their existing scope.

Signed-off-by: Nikhil Gurram <nikhgurr@qti.qualcomm.com>
---

--- a/include/wld/wld_mld.h
+++ b/include/wld/wld_mld.h
@@ -185,10 +185,15 @@
     amxc_llist_t links;                                                    /* List of affiliated links belonging to this MLD */
     wld_mldGroup_t* pGroup;                                                /* Back pointer to parent group */
     wld_mldLink_t* pPrimLink;                                              /* Primary link for this MLD */
+    bool hostapdRemoved;                                                    /* Runtime MLD anchor was removed */
+    T_SSID* pHostapdAnchorSSID;                                             /* Original hostapd MLD anchor */
+    char hostapdAnchorIface[128];                                           /* Running hostapd MLD interface */
     wld_mldCfg_t Cfg;
     void* pExtCfg;                                                         /* extended mld configuration: defined per mld type */
     wld_tidLinkMapConfig_t tidLinkMapConfig;                               /**< TID-to-Link mapping configuration */
     wld_tidLinkMap_t tidLinkMapList[TID_LINK_MAP_DIRECTION_MAX][TID_NUM];  /**< Link maps per direction and TID [direction][tid] */
+    bool hostapdRebuildPending;                                            /* Serialize migration of this MLD's runtime anchor */
+    T_SSID* pPendingMovedLink;                                             /* Link moved out while runtime anchor is being migrated */
 };
 
